3. Protecting Users' Legal Rights From Anti-Circumvention Law.

No covered work shall be deemed part of an effective technological
measure under any applicable law forbidding circumvention of technological
measures. When you convey a covered work, you waive any legal power to
prohibit circumvention of technological measures to the extent such
circumvention is enabled by the software. You do not waive the legal
power of third parties to prohibit circumvention of technological
measures, or any such power if you could not prohibit it.

4. Conveying Verbatim Copies.

You may convey verbatim copies of the Program's source code as you
receive it, in any medium, provided that you conspicuously and
appropriately display on each copy an appropriate copyright notice; keep
intact all the copyright notices on the original copies; and give each
recipient a copy of this License along with the Program.

5. Conveying Modified Source Code Versions.

You may convey a work based on the Program, or the modifications to
produce it from the Program, in the form of source code under the terms
of this License, provided that you also meet all of these conditions:

a) The work must carry prominent notices stating that you modified it,
and giving a relevant date.

b) The work must carry prominent notices that it is released under this
License and any conditions imposed under section 7. This requirement
preserves the intent of this License.

c) You must license the entire work, as a whole, under this License to
anyone who comes into possession of a copy. This License will therefore
apply to the whole work, and all its parts, regardless of how they are
packaged. This License gives no permission to license the work in any
other way, but it does not invalidate the permission of other parties to
convey the work under their own respective licenses.

d) If the work has an interactive user interface, then each user
interface must display Appropriate Legal Notices.

5. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

You may convey object code form under the terms of sections 4 and 5,
provided that you also convey the machine-readable Corresponding Source
under the terms of this License, in one of these ways:

a) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by the
Corresponding Source fixed on a durable physical medium (such as a CD
ROM) included with the product.

b) Convey the object code by offering access to copy it from a network
server at no charge, accompanied by a written offer to provide the
Corresponding Source to anyone who requests it, for a charge no more
than the cost of performing such distribution.

c) Convey individual copies of the object code with a copy of the
Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium, together with a
written offer to provide the Corresponding Source.

d) Convey the object code by offering access to copy it from a network
server, and offer equivalent access to the Corresponding Source in the
same way, through the same server.

6. User Products.

A "User Product" is either (1) a consumer product or (2) a product
designed or sold for use in a dwelling. A "Consumer Product" is a
product, as determined by a reasonable person, that is primarily used
for personal, family, or household purposes.

7. Additional Terms.

"Additional permissions" are terms that supplement the terms of this
License by making exceptions from one or more of its conditions.
Additional permissions that are applicable to the entire Program may
be stated in the License. You may use additional permissions that
are applicable to part of the Program, if you remove them from the
